==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|finicking}}, from {{m|en|finical}}, from {{m|en|fine}}. Compare {{m|en|finikin}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfɪnɪki/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[fastidious|Fastidious]] and [[fussy]]; difficult to [[please]]; [[exacting]], especially about [[detail]]s.
#: ''The baby was '''finicky''' until her diaper was changed.
# {{lb|en|informal}} Demanding, requiring above-normal care.
#: ''The lawnmower is a bit '''finicky''' in cold weather.''

====Usage notes====
* The forms {{m|en|finickier}} and {{m|en|finickiest}} also exist, but are quite rare, and perhaps nonstandard. The forms {{m|en||more finicky}} and {{m|en||most finicky}} are much more common, and certainly standard.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|fastidious}}, {{l|en|fussy}}
* See [[wikisaurus:fastidious]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|finickiness}}
* {{l|en|finickity}}

